    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d185">

                <pb facs="0357" n="285" sameAs="frus:frus1882/pg285"/>

                <head>No. 130.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Lowell to Mr.
                    Frelinghuysen</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1882-07-19"><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi> 19, 1882</date>.
                        (Received August 2.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 402.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to my dispatch No. 393, of 10th
                    instant, and to my cable dispatch of the 11th instant, in which I stated that
                    the only alleged American citizens now imprisoned in Ireland are O’Mahoney,
                    Sweeney, Slattery, and Gannon, I have the honor to acquaint you that I received
                    yesterday a letter from Mr. Barrows, the consul at Dublin, <pb facs="0358"
                        n="286" xml:id="pg286"/> from which it appears that Mr. William Brophy is
                    still a prisoner in Naas jail, and that Lord Granville was mistaken in stating
                    he had been released. I am unable to explain this discrepancy.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">* * * * * * *</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>J. R. LOWELL.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
